@format 1
@id keyframes.previous
@title Move to previous keyframe
@area 3. Keyframes and waveform
@entry input
@summary Resolve the latest stored keyframe before the cursor and move immediately when any candidate exists, without first confirming that the cursor region has been scanned.
@section II. Functionality
@flow TB
@related keyframes.scan, keyframes.next, keyframes.nearest

@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow
@alias key = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LKeyframeOrchestrator

[input] Previous-keyframe command <input>
- Dispatch the previous-keyframe shortcut when timeline commands and a spool are active @ flow.PFlowShortcutDispatch(...)
> find

[find] Search stored keyframes <decision>
- Search the entire stored keyframe set for the greatest timestamp strictly before the cursor @ key.LKeyframeMoveFind(...)
- Return that stored timestamp without checking whether the span around the current cursor has been scanned @ key.LKeyframeMoveFind(...)
? "Any earlier stored keyframe exists" > move
? "No earlier stored keyframe exists" > defer

[move] Move to stored candidate <process>
- Accept the non-null stored candidate and propagate it as the new cursor @ flow.PFlowKeyframeMove(...)
- Update both timeline views, request a scan around the new position, and seek the preview @ flow.PFlowCursorPropagate(...)
> result

[result] Previous stored keyframe selected <output>
= The cursor may move to a remote previously scanned region when the current cursor region has not been scanned.

[defer] Request scanning near current cursor <process>
- Defer a keyframe scan around the unchanged cursor only when no earlier stored candidate exists @ flow.PFlowKeyframeMove(...)
- Start the delayed scan request @ flow.PFlowKeyframeDefer(...)
> map:keyframes.scan
